ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "2.7.0", text = "More control over how your bars, XP bar and minimap fade, and a sign pointing at the options that were there all along.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Edit Mode: yes, FlareUI has more options. No, they didn't go anywhere. They've been in Edit Mode this whole time, behind the buttons that say Edit, which take you right to them. Since those buttons turned out to be a little too subtle, the Unit Frames and Action Bars pages now have a banner saying so, with an |cffffffffOpen Edit Mode|r button. Edit Mode itself now tells you to click a FlareUI frame the first time you open it. You've got this.\n• Action bars, XP bar: each one now has its own |cffffffffFade Speed|r and |cffffffffMin Alpha|r in Edit Mode, so a bar can fade to see-through instead of disappearing.\n• Fade groups: |cffffffffFade group|r is now the top option, and a group shares its Show Condition, Fade Speed and Min Alpha. Pick a group to see what's set for it. A change from any bar in the group applies to all of them.\n• Minimap: it can now fade too, with Show Condition and Fade Speed in Edit Mode. It fades on its own, all the way out, because the game won't let addons fade the player arrow or quest marks.\n• Party frames: your own frame in the party now shows the Five-Second Rule spark when the player frame has it on.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Fade Player and Pet: now one percentage, below Colour Palette, choosing how far the frames fade. 100% is no fading. If you were already fading, it shows 0%, the same as before.\n• Action bars: Fade Speed moved from the settings page to each bar in Edit Mode. Your old speed stays until you change it.\n• Edit Mode: bar, XP bar and minimap options now sit under a |cffffffffVisibility|r title.\n\n|cffffd100Removed|r\n• Minimap: Map Size is gone, as it didn't work well. The map goes back to its default size. Use Edit Mode's Scale to resize the whole minimap." },
    { version = "2.6.2", text = "A fix for errors when changing fonts.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Fonts: picking a font that won't load no longer causes errors, as it did on the Buffs & Debuffs page. That text uses Friz Quadrata instead, in every module." },
    { version = "2.6.1", text = "A fix for the round minimap showing inside the square one.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: Forever's round map frame no longer shows inside the square minimap when another addon tints it, as BetterBlizzFrames does at every login." },
    { version = "2.6.0", text = "Pet frames in your frame style, portraits you can click, and the option to hide your player frame while in a party.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Pet frame: in FlareUI Style and Forever Style the pet frame now follows your style, as a small version of your player frame. Your old pet frame settings are kept: turn on |cffffffffSimple Pet Frame|r in Unit Frames > Look to go back to the plain frame. Addon Style keeps the plain frame.\n• Party frames: |cffffffffHide Player Frame while in party|r, below Show Player in Edit Mode. Your player and pet frames hide while you're in a party, and come back solo and in a raid. Your frame in the party has the same right-click menu.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit Frames settings: every option in this section now applies to all styles, including Fade Player and Pet, colours, names, auras and fonts. The values from the style you're using now become the ones used everywhere.\n• Unit Frames settings: Full Player Names now sits above Class Colours.\n• Party and boss frames: the default Spacing is 14 in every style. Spacing you already have stays as it is.\n• FlareUI Totems: new default positions, sizes and totems per row in FlareUI Style and Forever Style. Totems you've already set up stay as they are.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Portraits and level discs in FlareUI Style and Forever Style now work like the rest of the frame: click to select, right-click for the menu, hover for the tooltip, and click casting and pings.\n• Minimap: a problem elsewhere during startup can no longer leave a round map inside the square frame." },
    { version = "2.5.4", text = "A clean edge for the minimap.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: the map no longer pokes out past the border art at its right-hand corners." },
